{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like","id":1292916,"title":"Nation state whose primary economy is medical care - how would it look like?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-28T19:54:32-08:00","id":1292916,"title":"Nation state whose primary economy is medical care - how would it look like?","content":"OK. Let's say that a sorcerer sets up shop in the hundred kingdoms. The kingdom has nothing. No mines. No great farmland. Just some very nice and interesting herbs.<br /> <br /> So what does the sorcerer do? He begins summoning Sesseljae, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_QFNIhwPiUw15ghFEG48Z1WvcRt3HNCvIAx1OaxnefE/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_QFNIhwPiUw15ghFEG48Z1WvcRt3HNCvIAx1OaxnefE/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_QFNIhwPiUw15ghFEG48Z1WvcRt3HNCvIAx1OaxnefE/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_QFNIhwPiUw15ghFEG48Z1WvcRt3HNCvIAx1OaxnefE/mobilebasic </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-514#post-4539601\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-514#post-4539601\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-514#post-4539601\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-514#post-4539601 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I just want to point out, the whole Yelled At By The CEO thing I mentioned? That's not a snarky quip, that literally happened to Magic R&amp;D after the production of the infamously broken and overpowered Urza's Saga set that nearly killed the game dead because it literally snapped the meta in two... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Aideara, the Sky-Sewn Brides<br /> Demon of the First Circle<br /> Progeny of the Meteoric Twins<br /> The aideara are inhumanly beautiful women, idealised copies of the form Kinmaya's lover wore in life. To look at them is almost to fall in love, and it takes a cruel heart or an iron will to raise a hand against one. If one looks closely, the delicate tracery of stitches running across their bodies is visible, like an intricate web of tattoos which accentuate and emphasise their beauty rather than detract from it. Few find themselves in the position to make this discovery, however, for the sky-sewn brides love only Kinmaya, and to love or have sex with another is an Unacceptable Order to them. For all their beauty, they are chaste, and will not consensually accept intimacy with another.<br /> <br /> Aideara share one mind in many parts, the transferred consciousness of the woman who Kinmaya fell for in times long past. The love between the Brides and their creator burns strong to this day, and every aideara has a Motivation simply of &quot;Love Kinmaya&quot;. She gave her lover more than immortality when she made a race of First Circles from her, though. The aideara are accomplished medics, gifted with the same skill and patient knowledge that allowed Kinmaya to create them in turn. Sewing severed limbs back on, transplanting failing organs or treating trauma wounds from battle comes as naturally to the Sky-Sewn Brides as breathing, and no mortal can match their talent.<br /> <br /> Although they may be First Circle demons, they have the heart of one of the Second Circle, and they are, one and all, citizens, for Kinmaya spends much political capital, and gives greatly to the Priests of Cecelyne for such respect to be afforded. Even if that were not true, though, the aideara share a mind, and they do act to revenge themselves should any inhabitant of Malfeas offer discourtesy to any one of them. In this, they show a remnant of the woman they were crafted from, an edge of her sharpness and wit, which they do not show around their lover and creator.<br /> <br /> Summoning: (Obscurity 2/3) These demons are often summoned as medics, for transplants or battlefield treatments. In the last five years, they have also been summoned to serve as necrosurgeons, and that they perform with the same calm contentment as they do the repair of an arm. In addition, their collective mind has seen many things, although compared to the teodozija, they are much younger, and have their origin in the Age of Sorrows. Sometimes, when a woman has lived a chaste life of unrequited love, one will be called to her when she dies. Then they will take her apart, and sew their own flesh into her, making a new sister-self from her remains, the old memories added, dimly remembered, to the collective, while they all enjoy the pure love of their beloved. They can also be called out of Malfeas by the tears of such a woman; in those cases, the Bride offers to make her beautiful and give her love unending. If an agreement is made, the woman is smothered by dexterous hands, and remade. Summoners who wish to enjoy their beauty may do so, but from a distance; any attempt to engage in sexual contact with one will cause it to gain one point of Limit an action, and unless ordered to be silent, they will object most strenuously.<br /> <br /> Motivation: Love Kinmaya<br /> <br /> Virtues: Compassion 5, Conviction 5, Temperance 5, Valour 4<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength 2, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Charisma 3, Manipulation 3, Appearance 7, Intelligence 3, Wits 3, Perception 4<br /> <br /> Abilities: Melee 1 (Surgical Tools + 1, In Defence of One's Virtue +2), Integrity 4 (Remaining Faithful +3), Performance 3 (Singing +1, With Kinmaya +2), Presence 2 (Inhuman Beauty +3), Resistance 4 (Resisting Diseases +3), Survival 2, Craft (Air) 3, Craft (Fire) 2, Investigation 1, Lore 2 (Eastern Folk Tales +1, Methods of Life Extension +2), Medicine 6 (Repairing Flesh +1), Occult 5 (Demonology +1, Second Circle Demons +2), Athletics 3, Awareness 2, Dodge 2 (Against Grapples +3), Linguistics 5 (Forest Tongue, Old Realm, plus others), Socialise 3 (Polite Distance +1)<br /> <br /> Backgrounds: Backing 3 (Kinmaya)<br /> <br /> Thaumaturgy: The Aideara have a Master-level degree in the Art of Demon Summoning, and will instruct others in it; notably, they know \u201cBeckon Kinmaya\u201d, and will preferentially teach that to anyone who asks. They are also versed in the Art of Elemental Summoning, the Art of Geomancy, and although they do not make this knowledge available, the Art of the Dead.<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> Divine (Medicine) Subordination \u2013 Only on acts of surgery and other kinds of flesh crafting and sewing; it can be used to graft a hand from a fresh corpse onto a person and make it work, but it cannot be used to diagnose or treat disease.<br /> Materialise<br /> Benefaction \u2013 Blesses rolls to recover from injury or fight off infection<br /> Touch of Grace \u2013 Only to heal, leaves thin scars which do not heal as a Crippling effect. Healing Crippling Effects requires access to spare body parts, which are used in the repair.<br /> Shapechange \u2013 May convert her hands into any tools needed for surgery or medical operations.<br /> Portal \u2013 To the side of the most injured, still-living person within 10 miles, and affects its user with an irresistible Compulsion to do everything in their power to save the patient.<br /> Divine Perogative \u2013 To remain faithful to Kinmaya<br /> Plague of Menaces \u2013 Other aideara, and, via a contract of Kinmaya with Alevua, the insects of Malfeas.<br /> Second (Ability) Excellency \u2013 Medicine, Integrity, Performance, Resistance<br /> Third (Ability) Excellency \u2013 Medicine, Integrity, Occult<br /> <br /> Join Battle: 5<br /> Attacks:<br /> Medical Implements: Speed 5, Accuracy 9, Damage 5L, PDV 3, Rate 3<br /> Soak: 1L/6B (Perfect Skin +0L/+3B)<br /> Health Levels: -0/ -0/ -0/ -2 / -4/ -4 /-4/Incap<br /> Dodge DV: 3 (5 against grapples) Willpower: 8<br /> Essence: 4 Essence Pool: 80<br /> <br /> Other notes: Much like the teodozija, the aideara share one mind, though they are bound less tightly. With a successful difficulty 4 (Intelligence + Lore) roll by the demon\u2019s player, the sky-sewn bride may briefly access the aideara shared mind to learn any information relevant to a situation at hand that is known by any other aideara, or, at difficulty 5, that was known by any mortal woman who was made into a sky-sewn bride. An aideara will tend to accumulate fresh body parts, which, by an application of her saliva, she stops from rotting, which she will use in her medical repairs, and will collect parts from any patients she cannot save to use on ones that she can. They have a refined sense of aesthetics, and so will attempt to make the best match of a part to their current patient, but it is not uncommon to find that a patient now has one arm a different colour to, and more muscular than, the other one. The aideara may only use fresh body parts; ones where rot has set in are useless to them.<br /> <br /> OK. So the kingdom now has the best doctors and health care for miles around. How would this look like? <br /> <br /> For me, I'll think that whatever farmland they have to be repurposed and be sent to cultivating medicinal herbs and plants. When the biggest game in town is doctoring and medicine, why not sell stuff that profits from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T20:34:09-08:00","id":1292927,"title":"","content":"You've got doctors, but how are you getting patients?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T20:47:32-08:00","id":1292928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292927#post1292927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've got doctors, but how are you getting patients?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mass tourism, attempted construction of roadworks?<br /> <br /> Battles as wounded enemies on different sides find each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T20:51:37-08:00","id":1292929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292928#post1292928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mass tourism, attempted construction of roadworks?<br /> <br /> Battles as wounded enemies on different sides find each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>But if a person is sick or injured enough to need this care, how are they undertaking the journey?<br /> <br /> For that matter, what kinds of costs are they going to face if they can make it there alive?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T21:03:18-08:00","id":1292931,"title":"","content":"Kinda reminds me of Kharbranth from the Stormlight Archive. It makes it's money by selling access to the biggest library in the world and then funnels that money into free hospitals. This also means that every doctor worth their salt pays to study in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6585-nightshrike","name":"nightshrike","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T21:04:23-08:00","id":1292932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292929#post1292929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if a person is sick or injured enough to need this care, how are they undertaking the journey?<br /> <br /> For that matter, what kinds of costs are they going to face if they can make it there alive?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... <br /> <br /> Personally, I would like to say that there is a scaling pay scale. The wealthier you are. The more you pay.<br /> <br /> .... More likely, they will either do indentured servitude, or ruinous debt. <br /> <br /> As for injuries... They don't. Or they're rich and can afford it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T21:27:28-08:00","id":1292936,"title":"","content":"Itinerant doctors, exaltified pharmaceutical sales and franchized hospitals are also options for revenue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T21:56:06-08:00","id":1292944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292932#post1292932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for injuries... They don't. Or they're rich and can afford it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the issue that traveling while you're sick or injured is itself pretty hazardous. Being rich doesn't negate the potential for a bump in the road to aggravate a wound enough to reopen it and cause you to bleed out before you reach your destination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T22:38:07-08:00","id":1292948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292944#post1292944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing the issue that traveling while you're sick or injured is itself pretty hazardous. Being rich doesn't negate the potential for a bump in the road to aggravate a wound enough to reopen it and cause you to bleed out before you reach your destination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. <br /> <br /> When I said injuries, I was thinking about broken legs that didn't heal properly. Or injured tendons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T23:49:15-08:00","id":1292956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JiveX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292936#post1292936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Itinerant doctors, exaltified pharmaceutical sales and franchized hospitals are also options for revenue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Travelling doctors? <br /> <br /> As for Exaltified.... Um.... yeah. My idea for this is that its relatively low powered. No exalted. Maybe a few god and demon blooded. <br /> <br /> The idea for this entire story was the thought about how resource trap ruins countries and economies. And how the sudden influx of money to Venezuela caused it to become rife with corruption, hamstringing its development. I'm wondering how having doctors and the being amongst the best hospitals in Creation would change things. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T00:05:14-08:00","id":1292958,"title":"","content":"So, the closest historical analogue would be medieval shrines famed for healing.<br /> <br /> People would travel from far and wide to come, often brought by their families due to the difficulty of traveling while sick.<br /> <br /> And of course, they need roads, accommodation, food... A whole tourism industry, essentially.<br /> <br /> But thinking of your demon based model... How many demons? Presumably not thousands. Does the charge rise to meet demand? Do the rich come and get treated,while the poor and desperate become bandits to get the money?<br /> <br /> It's interesting. But that's about health tourism.<br /> <br /> If you are interested in the resource trap, I'd think more about the ownership model. Who controls the demons? Who gets the revenue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T00:15:29-08:00","id":1292960,"title":"","content":"Demons? A hundred. Definitely not more than a two hundred. Task bound, or commanded by the sorcerer. <br /> <br /> I'm also planning a manse that specializes in growing medicinal herbs. Grows them well. Grows them fast. Boosts their efficacy. But also makes them useless for anything else. <br /> <br /> Resource trap? Maybe I can have the sorcerer bind them in specified rooms or houses. Then tell them. &quot;Heal whomever enters.&quot; Anyone owning those rooms or buildings, gets a ready source of income. A source of income that will probably never deplete, cause even in a recession, doctors are laid off last. So... battle for ownership of these buildings is fierce. Both politically, and.. physically. <br /> <br /> As for the charge, I'm not sure. I'm sure that you can create a plot hook where you can have the medical fees increase the richer you are. So making people get pissed off, cause they feel its unfair. Cue a conspiracy between rich merchants and princes, that wish to oust the sorcerer and take the facilities for themselves. Or have a plot hook about unfortunate poor people forced into ruinous debt by the prices, thus triggering either social change, or a bad guy to fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T03:22:51-08:00","id":1292974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nightshrike</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292931#post1292931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda reminds me of Kharbranth from the Stormlight Archive. It makes it's money by selling access to the biggest library in the world and then funnels that money into free hospitals. This also means that every doctor worth their salt pays to study in the city.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seconding this. I don't know how well this meshes with demons, but if the nation gets a reputation for quality doctors, other nations will want to send their medical practitioners for training. They might even be able to lease their doctors (and demons) for their neighbours for a price.<br /> They could also have treatment facilities for incurable, but not immediately lethal diseases. Think how tuberculosis used to be dealt with: nobility sent their sick to resort-like facilities to get treatment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","user":"Taleksi","date":".  Removed some errant words. 03-01-2019, 06:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24320-taleksi","name":"Taleksi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24320_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T04:06:34-08:00","id":1292980,"title":"","content":"Wow. Cancer. Fertility problems. Plastic surgery. Leprosy. Pregnancy. <br /> <br /> That's... A lot of potential stuff. So hotels. The rich, high end kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T04:25:46-08:00","id":1292982,"title":"","content":"First thing to notice is that natural resources are not the only path to wealth. So a barren place can still be viable or rich, as long as whatever they do is worth enough that the people there can earn enough to just buy whatever else from outside. So your demon-hospital city can be viable if that's all it has outstanding to offer.<br /> <br /> Geography's your first, and maybe biggest, obstacle. Whenever people have to travel to get what they want things get expensive, fast. Anywhere farther than a couple days of travel is a huge endeavour. In the hundred kingdoms area means you have a few hundred thousand people that may be able to afford that much travel to visit. Plenty for most commerce, especially if it establishes itself as a major buyer and the bigger caravans find profit.<br /> <br /> Probably far less for treatment, though, as the ill are not exactly easy to lug around.<br /> <br /> So, outside the town itself you'll probably not find viable markets unless the doctors themselves can travel, at which point you have to ask how you will bind them to your desired place to profit.<br /> Itinerant doctors and affiliated hospitals contract-bound to pay you a portion of their gains is a good bet. as that expands your reach to how far your doctors can go. With healer demons that's probably the whole eastern threshold.<br /> <br /> Now you have to ponder other factors, like reputation and control. How do you get around the fact demons are fucking creepy? How do you keep the demons in their best behavior? Even those already inclined to do what you want them to do will still do and want troublesome things. The immaculate doctrine probably wouldn't like an established demonic hospital tradition, too, as that's going to be very inviting to foster infernalist cults.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T04:31:07-08:00","id":1292984,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... <br /> <br /> 1) these sort of extreme specializations tend to work best in regions where extensive trade and mobility are backed by an integrated market and relative peace. otoh, I think you can treat that a bit loosely in spirit (since X-country is a fantasy thing and we do have states like Sijan already).<br /> <br /> medical exports and medical tourism are doable, but you need a very well integrated trade system before people are going to start totally moving away from subsistence wherever they are in favour of trading for food (because any disruptions to your trade system and you can't fall back on the food you produce). it also makes you very vulnerable to blockading by whatever local strongman thug sees that you may have some seizable surplus.<br /> <br /> (why a lot of the specialisation that makes high economic growth possible was dependent on development of relative degrees of peace and states with limits on increases in taxes, etc.)<br /> <br /> 2) it might be nice to have some sort of baked in geographical advantage for the city; favourable geomancy and astrological blessings, left over First Age magic, or magic hot springs, something like this, to help explain why this place has an advantage over distributed those services more naturally, as tends to be the case IRL (medical care tends to be internationally non-traded, barring some medical tourism). but you say it has nothing so I guess that's out?<br /> <br /> Might be best to place this state in a more stable part of the Hundred Kingdoms (though not too far, as med care is complementary to violence?).<br /> <br /> If it's a long term project, perhaps he needs to use diplomacy and alliances with other local powers to develop some kind of binding norms and traditions against attacking them? Or a good relationship with some local mercenaries, where it's not credible that you can become surplus to their requirements and be betrayed by them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T05:58:28-08:00","id":1292995,"title":"","content":"Historically there are analogs. It is basically tourism, but the people are there to be healed rather than see a particular set of paintings or hear a particular performer.<br /> <br /> Hospitality would be the primary industry in the area.<br /> <br /> The first thing I thought about was Yharnam from Bloodborne with its Cathedral Ward.<br /> <br /> Depending on how your game goes there could also be a rousing prostitution business as well because social diseases would be all but unheard of. You might even have some daemons that cater strictly to that if you wanted to go that route. <br /> <br /> I actually think this is a pretty great idea and one that could be fleshed out in a variety of directions. For players, it could even be a honeypot Lotus-Eater Machine type of scenario for them or even an epiphanic prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:02:50-08:00","id":1292996,"title":"","content":"Ooh.... Maybe extra services? Ya know. Neomah babies and all. Detox. Having access to Sesseljae means that you can shoot yourself up with any kind of drug or wine, then still be alive and sober the next day.<br /> <br /> Maybe they come for the aidera? Appearance 7 does a lot... <br /> <br /> Question. How does one mechanically represent plastic surgery in Creation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:26:00-08:00","id":1293000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292996#post1292996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh.... Maybe extra services?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that no matter how big a business is, if people gravitate to it just about every other business will crop up, as those peoples have wants and needs.<br /> Entertainment will crop up, fast.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:29:46-08:00","id":1293004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293000#post1293000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that no matter how big a business is, if people gravitate to it just about every other business will crop up, as those peoples have wants and needs.<br /> Entertainment will crop up, fast.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Um... yes? I live in Singapore. <br /> <br /> You gotta get people to come to you. We got it by banking, shipping, industry, and other stuff. <br /> <br /> Why not medicine? Especially since sorcerers and friendly medicinal demons are rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:30:41-08:00","id":1293005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1292995#post1292995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first thing I thought about was Yharnam from Bloodborne with its Cathedral Ward.<br /> <br /> I actually think this is a pretty great idea and one that could be fleshed out in a variety of directions. For players, it could even be a honeypot Lotus-Eater Machine type of scenario for them or even an epiphanic prison.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never played bloodborne. But I've heard of it. Tell me more about this 'Cathedral ward'. <br /> <br /> Please explain what you mean by 'honeypot' or 'epiphanic prison'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:43:31-08:00","id":1293008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293004#post1293004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um... yes? I live in Singapore.<br /> <br /> You gotta get people to come to you. We got it by banking, shipping, industry, and other stuff.<br /> <br /> Why not medicine? Especially since sorcerers and friendly medicinal demons are rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err...is this a reply to a disagreement? I thought we were in agreement, all the way. Sorry, this got a bit confused.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:47:22-08:00","id":1293009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293008#post1293008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err...is this a reply to a disagreement? I thought we were in agreement, all the way. Sorry, this got a bit confused.</div> </div> </div> </div>An agreement. <br /> <br /> I know. Isn't this kinda obvious? Does it really need saying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T06:52:02-08:00","id":1293011,"title":"","content":"Gotcha. I tried to expand on it. Apparently, I failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:04:40-08:00","id":1293013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293011#post1293011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotcha. I tried to expand on it. Apparently, I failed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. No worries about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:06:54-08:00","id":1293016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293005#post1293005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never played bloodborne. But I've heard of it. Tell me more about this 'Cathedral ward'.</div> </div> </div> </div>From memory in Bloodborne the entire city of Yharnam existed because there was a church that had the blood of the great old ones that could cure any illness. The Cathedral ward was where people went for those services. The Healing Church is in this district of the city. (It turns out that the blood of the old ones has some unintended consequences. . . so the city is basically on fire and inhabited by monsters when the game starts)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293005#post1293005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please explain what you mean by 'honeypot' or 'epiphanic prison'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw that you live in Singapore, so I don't want to assume cultural knowledge. Please don't assume that I am talking down to you if you know Winnie the Pooh then my explanation may appear a bit banal.<br /> <br /> Honeypot was named for a trope involving something looking inviting only to be a trap. This happens often to a fictitious character named Winnie the Pooh who finds pots full of honey and after sticking his head into the pots to eat all of the honey will get his head stuck inside of the pot. The concept is also known as a &quot;honey trap&quot; though and it is when a very attractive deal is presented that is &quot;too good to pass up.&quot; Often times it is a sexy woman who then lures men back to be robbed or blackmailed or whatever, but it can take many forms. If you have played Dragon Quest XI the cursed mural in the town of Phnom Nohn is a good example of this trope (the one that culminates by fighting Dora in Grey.)<br /> <br /> An epiphanic prison is a variant on the Lotus-Eater Machine where the players have to have an epiphany in order to escape. Not every prison has walls, and sometimes victory is borning. If the villain can win by just stalling out the heroes then a Lotus-Eater Machine can work really well to do that. The epiphany can just be that the town is a trap or that they are all psychic vampires or something.<br /> <br /> IIRC there was a story in the old Assamite clanbook about the Viziers achieving enlightenment using drugs that involved a similar scenario.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:24:06-08:00","id":1293019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293016#post1293016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From memory in Bloodborne the entire city of Yharnam existed because there was a church that had the blood of the great old ones that could cure any illness. The Cathedral ward was where people went for those services. The Healing Church is in this district of the city. (It turns out that the blood of the old ones has some unintended consequences. . . so the city is basically on fire and inhabited by monsters when the game starts).</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Yharnam existed before they found the blood but the blood did alter them as a society. It wasn't just a psudo cure, the blood formed a religion and the people gathered around it. It also wasn't a religion at first but a group of scholars.<br /> <br /> Places of healing can inspire traversal but that's usually limited to monuments. A town of healers would be mostly worthless. The church was just a small if central part of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:31:53-08:00","id":1293021,"title":"","content":"So... Transport. He's a sorcerer. How about building highways using raising the earth's bones or a demon?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-887#post-5867233\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-887#post-5867233\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-887#post-5867233\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-887#post-5867233 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> It's a commodity based system. Any excess in the balance of silver will be either saved, and thus taken out of the system, or traded away, where the impact is much reduced. And big enough chunks to crash the economy would be in the realm of 20%+ of the entire economy, which is such a weight of... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Sadakeeda, The Brass Caterpillars, Demon of the First Circle.<br /> The basalt roads of Jacint criss-cross the many layer of Malfeas, forming the backbone that connects the demon city. However, these roads are never connected to each other, or the plates, in ways that are comprehensible to mortals or the less serfs of the city. Created in order to connect the many paths of Jacint, the Sadakeeda have found a home among all the demon city, and are used to carve paths for trade, and for war. Octavian is know to keep a stable of the creatures, bred to be especially voracious, for use as siege engines, as they simply eat their way through fortification, while leaving a path for his army to follow.<br /> <br /> Each Sadakeeda appears as a massive caterpillar, the size of a Yeddim, with it's segmented shell made of a golden brass alloy; though the shine of the shell is rarely visible, due to the nature of the beast. As it crawls along the plates of Malfeas, it consumes all in front of it, via it's massive gaping maw, lined with many spinning circles of teeth. Inside the worm, a massive vat of vitriol and fire breaks down all the consumed materials in to a dark bituminous pitch, save stones, which are broken down into a mix of gravel and sand. This mix is extruded out between the massive golden plates, staining a shining creature black and slimy, and fills the trench the Caterpillar leaves behind. Over the next several hours, this slime hardens to a smooth, black rock-like structure, similar to the basalt roads of Jacint, though much softer, but still convenient to travel upon.<br /> <br /> Due to it's lack of eyes, Sadakeeda will only travel travel in strait lines, consuming all within their path. When used in the demon city, care must be taken be taken to ensure that they don't eat their way through anything of value.<br /> <br /> Only two things redirect or stop a hungry Sadakeeda. Should the Brass Caterpillars encounder a stream of flowing water, it will stop upon the slightest touch, for the waters of creation and Kimbery are toxic to the Sadakeeda. Should it be tricked into consuming more than a bucket full of water, it enters a form of torpor, freezing in place until it is fed at least a buckets worth of burning coals, or burning charcoals. The other thing that can redirect the worm is the scent of it's favorite food, coal. Should the Brass Caterpillar scent coal nearby, it will divert it's path to eat all of the black rock that it can fit into it's mouth.<br /> <br /> Given enough coal to eat, The Brass Caterpillars will enter a form of cocoon, wrapping itself in a stone shell, which will them grow red hot from within. After 1 month spend in this form, the shell will shatter open, revealing a collection of smaller Brass Caterpillars, each which set out on their own path.<br /> <br /> A Brass Caterpillar can escape into creation whenever a man dies of thirst or starvation, while traveling down a road.<br /> <br /> Summoning: Sadakeeda are summoned to carve paths throughout creation, though they are of less use in some areas, due to the amount of water. Sorcerers who summon the worms will mark the path they wish the Sadakeeda to follow with clusters of burning coals, guiding down a path not to steep for human travel, and away from rivers, puddles, and springs that might stall the worm. They have been used as siege weapons as well, eating their way through the walls of castles and cities.<br /> <br /> Motivation: To satiate it's endless hunger.<br /> <br /> Attributes: Strength: 12 Dexterity: 2 Stamina: 12 Charisma: 1 Manipulation: 1 Appearance: 4 (2 when coated with pitch) Perception: 1 Intelligence: 2 Wits: 3<br /> Virtues: Compassion 2, Conviction 5, Temperance 1, Valor 4<br /> Abilities: Athletics 5, Awareness 2(+3 Smelling), Craft (Earth) 1 (+3 Earthworks), Integrity 3, Investigation 1, Martial Arts 2 (+3 Bite), Melee 3, Occult 1, Presence 2, Resistance 5 (+2 Endure Hardship), Survival 2<br /> <br /> Charms:<br /> AFFINITY (ELEMENT) CONTROL \u2013 The Sadakeeda may control the bituminous pitch it extrudes<br /> BREAD OF WEAK SPIRIT \u2013 The Sadakeeda loves the taste of weaker gods.<br /> DOMAIN MANIPULATION SCENARIO \u2013 The Sadakeeda can twist the roadway it leaves behind.<br /> ESSENCE BITE --- The burning tar that covers the Sadakeeda is unpleasant to touch.<br /> Materialize\u2014Costs 60 motes<br /> Ox body Technique x3\u200b<br /> Tracking \u2013 May only track coal, or a bound location.<br /> Landscape Travel --- The Sadakeeda can crawl across almost any surface, or even up walls.<br /> First (Ability) Excellency\u2014Athletics, Craft, Resistance\u200b<br /> Third (Ability) Excellency\u2014Athletics, Craft, Resistance<br /> <br /> Join Battle: 5<br /> Attacks:<br /> Bite: Speed 5, Accuracy 7, Damage 8L, Parry DV 0<br /> Trample: Speed 3, Accuracy 5, Damaged 12L<br /> Soak: 18B/14L (Malfean Brass Plates +12B/+8L)<br /> <br /> HL: -0x2/-1x3/-2x3/-4x3/I<br /> <br /> Willpower: 9 Essence: 3 Essence Pool: 70<br /> <br /> Other Notes: The Sadakeeda moves at rate of about 2 mph while traveling overland, leaving behind a trail of asphalt approximately 3 yards wide, level with the surrounding terrain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:38:50-08:00","id":1293023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293016#post1293016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From memory in Bloodborne the entire city of Yharnam existed because there was a church that had the blood of the great old ones that could cure any illness. The Cathedral ward was where people went for those services. The Healing Church is in this district of the city. (It turns out that the blood of the old ones has some unintended consequences. . . so the city is basically on fire and inhabited by monsters when the game starts)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I saw that you live in Singapore, so I don't want to assume cultural knowledge. Please don't assume that I am talking down to you if you know Winnie the Pooh then my explanation may appear a bit banal.<br /> <br /> Honeypot was named for a trope involving something looking inviting only to be a trap. This happens often to a fictitious character named Winnie the Pooh who finds pots full of honey and after sticking his head into the pots to eat all of the honey will get his head stuck inside of the pot. The concept is also known as a &amp;quot;honey trap&amp;quot; though and it is when a very attractive deal is presented that is &amp;quot;too good to pass up.&amp;quot; Often times it is a sexy woman who then lures men back to be robbed or blackmailed or whatever, but it can take many forms. If you have played Dragon Quest XI the cursed mural in the town of Phnom Nohn is a good example of this trope (the one that culminates by fighting Dora in Grey.)<br /> <br /> An epiphanic prison is a variant on the Lotus-Eater Machine where the players have to have an epiphany in order to escape. Not every prison has walls, and sometimes victory is borning. If the villain can win by just stalling out the heroes then a Lotus-Eater Machine can work really well to do that. The epiphany can just be that the town is a trap or that they are all psychic vampires or something.<br /> <br /> IIRC there was a story in the old Assamite clanbook about the Viziers achieving enlightenment using drugs that involved a similar scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... I know exactly what a honeypot is. We even have our own analogue. <br /> <br /> What I meant was, in what way is the town/ city a honeypot trap? Because that wasn't my intention.<br /> <br /> Like... Its meant to be benign. Its just that when you're in the bronze age, suddenly having something that gives you near modern medical service is something that acts like nice plot hooks are conflict instigators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:43:32-08:00","id":1293025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293019#post1293019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Yharnam existed before they found the blood but the blood did alter them as a society. It wasn't just a psudo cure, the blood formed a religion and the people gathered around it. It also wasn't a religion at first but a group of scholars.<br /> <br /> Places of healing can inspire traversal but that's usually limited to monuments. A town of healers would be mostly worthless. The church was just a small if central part of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, it has been a while, and the lore in the solesborne games has always been a bit hard for me to follow. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Phnom Nohn from Dragon Quest XI is likely a better example anyway as it is much more direct, and offers multiple &quot;lures.&quot; <br /> <br /> I respectfully disagree that a town of healers would be mostly worthless in Exalted. I think it would have exactly the worth the ST/Plot needed it to have. I think there are quite a 3-4 pretty great ways to go with the above ideas to put them into a game.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:46:13-08:00","id":1293029,"title":"","content":"Everyone: please remember Exalted is in the bronze age. Life is rather... Nasty there.<br /> <br /> Medicine is what we would charitably call 'not very advanced'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:47:51-08:00","id":1293031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293023#post1293023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... I know exactly what a honeypot is. We even have our own analogue.<br /> <br /> What I meant was, in what way is the town/ city a honeypot trap? Because that wasn't my intention.<br /> <br /> Like... Its meant to be benign. Its just that when you're in the bronze age, suddenly having something that gives you near modern medical service is something that acts like nice plot hooks are conflict instigators.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, it could be benign. It <span style=\"font-size:12px\">co</span>uld <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\">absolutely</span></span> </span>be played that way. <br /> <br /> It likely speaks a lot about me that I want to turn your idea about a benign idea about a city based solely on helping people into an antagonist of some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:48:40-08:00","id":1293032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Navar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293031#post1293031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, it could be benign. It <span style=\"font-size:12px\">co</span>uld <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#1d2129\">absolutely</span></span> </span>be played that way. <br /> <br /> It likely speaks a lot about me that I want to turn your idea about a benign idea about a city based solely on helping people into an antagonist of some fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>.... What were your plans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T08:34:10-08:00","id":1293044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293032#post1293032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> .... What were your plans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just spitballing really. <br /> <br /> The scenario that seems to be the simplest though would go like:<br /> <br /> Have the city look like paradise. Have everyone believe that the city is a paradise where sick people come from far and wide to visit and get better. Some people die there sure, but with so many sick people it is to be expected. <br /> <br /> Turns out there is a rogue god who is a life force/psychic energy vampire. They cure people, but they use the lure of the city to draw an everlasting supply of fresh victims to gather fresh souls/bodies/anguish/etc.<br /> <br /> If this is a minor encounter then the PCs uncover the real reason for the city and have to decide to kill the god or not. The god does do lots of good for lots of people, but a small number of people have to die for this to happen. This can be framed however you want. The hook could even bee someone one of the PCs has an intimate tie to becoming ill and the PCs hearing about this city where they can go to have their loved one healed.<br /> <br /> Or this can be the culmination of a story and when the PCs arrive the god has finally acquired the souls/bodies/anguish/etc. they need and now their MacGuffin is about to explode/empower them/etc. The PCs would have to fight through hordes of loyal subjects who believe that they are doing good protecting the healers or bestial mutants who have been infected by the healer.<br /> <br /> OR it could just be a Lotus-Eater Machine designed solely to be a city of healing and hedonism (like someone said no hangovers or overdoses and no worries about STDs) Fighting pits???? Sounds like a grand idea when there is little consequence of injury. The PCs could be on a mission with a time-sensitive element and this city could just be on the road there. They spend a few nights in the brothels, maybe a patron pays for them to have a couple of weeks at one of the best hotels. If they take the bait then their adversaries become stronger/achieve their goals/get an infinity stone/etc.<br /> <br /> Again there are a few ways this could go if you wanted to make the OP idea malevolent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5172-navar","name":"Navar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5172_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T10:40:44-08:00","id":1293085,"title":"","content":"Maybe you can draw some inspiration from Drum Island from One Piece.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T14:45:51-08:00","id":1293147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293085#post1293085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you can draw some inspiration from Drum Island from One Piece.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T17:17:59-08:00","id":1293193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293029#post1293029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everyone: please remember Exalted is in the bronze age. Life is rather... Nasty there.<br /> <br /> Medicine is what we would charitably call 'not very advanced'</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it in the Bronze Age? Iron and steel are frequently mentioned, the &quot;Triremes&quot; in the setting are far more advanced than any ships built in antiquity. There's a bunch of other things in the setting that are post-renaissance level technology, such as telescopes or clockwork.<br /> <br /> And even if it is Bronze Age, it's not like medicine advanced much at all until the 19th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24366-slarn","name":"Slarn!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24366_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T17:30:17-08:00","id":1293194,"title":"","content":"It's especially not as if there was exactly one standard of quality for medicinal practices worldwide at a given point in history. Some groups have had some pretty advanced ideas, while others were guilty of some very unhealthy practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T18:38:50-08:00","id":1293209,"title":"","content":"Alright fine then. This idea is a flop. I had no idea Creation had modern. Medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T18:49:39-08:00","id":1293210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293209#post1293209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had no idea Creation had modern. Medicine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't even resemble what I said, and you know it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T18:53:26-08:00","id":1293214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1292916-nation-state-whose-primary-economy-is-medical-care-how-would-it-look-like?p=1293210#post1293210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't even resemble what I said, and you know it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. You said advanced. How advanced? Can they undo necrosis and sepsis? What about infected wounds? Reconstructive surgery? What about antibiotics and anti inflammatory medicine? Do they wash their hands? What about brass and silver door handles? What about organ and blood transplants?<br /> <br /> When a bone is broken, how fast do they recover, if at all? Are they crippled for life or walk with a limp? Can they do skin grafts or remove cancer? <br /> <br /> If the answer to these is no, then it's not advanced medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T17:18:35-08:00","id":1294241,"title":"","content":"Note: This is the first time I'm writing a manse. This is probably not very good.<br /> <br /> Set in the lowlands, in the middle of a valley right next to a river, protected by two mountains, lies a manse. The aspect is Wood, and it is composed out of a mixture of green jade, wood, and glass. The manse is low-setting, a simple shrine without even a roof. Wood essence pulses through the jade and tints the glassy columns green, and at night, the manse glows in the dark. The river right beside it powers a water wheel, moving a prayer wheel inscribed with prayers to the gods of health, medicinal herbs, and doctors. Several guards patrol daily, never resting, spears at the ready, green lamellar armour shining in the sun.<br /> <br /> The manse is the valley's greatest asset, as well as its most notable feature. Set by a dragonblooded sorcerer as a source of thaumaturgical and alchemical supplies, and left unattended after his death by an infernal akuma, the manse has endured from since living memory. The manse allows the valley to create vast amounts of medical supplies, with a contract with the guild enabling them to sell it to a wider market than they could achieve themselves. A small tradition has sprung up, a native association of doctors and herbalists, taking advantage of one of Creation's best sources of medicinal plants to educate themselves and to practice producing medicines and alchemical supplies. They hope that, if they practice and improve enough, they can produce their own products and medicine and sell them at a higher price, instead of having to sell the guild the raw materials.<br /> <br /> <b>Manse powers: the blessing of doctors</b><br /> <br /> Within a 3 mile radius, all crops, plants, or herbs, with medicinal properties are enhanced. No matter their native climate, whether they belong in the western sea or the frozen North, can live there. The amount of medicine produced are triplicated, and any medicine, drug, or tincture is enhanced, adding 2 successes to any roll involving them. <br /> <br /> Drawback: This applies only to ones with medicinal properties. Any food crops, such as rice, wheat, or potatoes, do not grow well, appearing withered and stunted. Any plant product used as food, will taste bland, and has their nutritional value cut in half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}